		"The 70 regular cards were transcribed from their official Japanese Pokémon Card Game detail pages; each page URL and SHA-256 digest is listed below.",
		"The nine secret-numbered cards were checked against card scans in the cited independent checklist. Cards 071–075 match the gameplay text and stats of the cited regular BW7 cards; cards 076–079 use matching official gameplay records, with printed identity, rarity and illustrator checked against each scan.",
		"The independent checklists agree on 79 numbered cards (70 regular and nine secret). One checklist reports a regular rarity split of 34 Common, 21 Uncommon and 15 Rare; the official detail pages classify the regular cards as 34 Common, 20 Uncommon and 16 Rare. Card rarity in this import follows the official per-card records; both totals produce 79 when the nine secret cards are included.",
		"Each numbered card has first-edition and unlimited variants. The official regular rarity and printed secret rarity distinguish 54 normal cards from 25 holo cards; the independent edition listing reports 54 normal and 25 holo in each edition.",
		"SR maps to Ultra Rare and UR maps to Secret Rare following neighboring Japanese BW data. The evolution links for Charizard #077 and Blastoise #078 were checked against their card-face evolution stages because the official detail pages list multiple evolutionary relationships across the species. No marketplace IDs or unverified artwork URLs are included; secret scan URLs are provenance only."
	],
